Dear Dr. Chisom Ezenwachi,

I am submitting this sworn statement under oath in connection with the above arbitration. I
understand that my statement will be treated as evidence and evaluated alongside the other
materials in the arbitration record.

**My Role**

I am a PhD candidate at the Department of Biomedical Informatics, University of Toronto, supervised by
Tariq Saleem. During the period 2024–2026, I was the primary data harmonisation engineer for the
Cross-Ancestry GWAS Collaboration. My principal responsibility was the generation and quality
control of the harmonized intermediate datasets, including `harmonized_gwas_v2/`.

**The Integration Timeline**

To the best of my recollection and based on my review of the git commit history of the pipeline
repository, the integration of `harmonized_gwas_v2/` into the main cohort pipeline was completed
before my email of 7 March 2025. Specifically:

  I was instructed by Tariq Saleem to proceed with the integration prior to the date of my
  email exchange with him. The March 7 email was written retrospectively to document the
  instruction I had already received and acted upon. The git commit history of the pipeline
  repository is the authoritative record of when the integration actually occurred.

I want to be clear that I was acting under instruction from Tariq Saleem throughout this process.
I understood that the approval process was being managed at the PI level and that my role was
to execute the technical integration. I was not aware of any unresolved objection from
Aoife Ní Mhurchadha at the time I carried out the integration.

Regarding the commit history: I am aware that one of my commits relating to the `harmonized_gwas_v2`
integration was subsequently amended to show a different author. I do not know the full
circumstances of that amendment but can confirm that the original commit was mine. I understand
from the repository history that this amendment was made by Liang Jiewen at his request.

I am available to answer any questions the ombudsperson may have.

